{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/reviews/id1251568555"}, "name":{"label":"hdiagkenhxian"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2023-01-30T06:38:20-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"2022.11"}, "id":{"label":"9563982952"}, "title":{"label":"If you like listening to podcasts in chronological order, don’t get this."}, "content":{"label":"First of all, this could be a bug on my phone in particular because it seems crazy to me that the app really is intended to behave the way it does.\n\nThis seems like step one of programming a podcast app, play episodes in order. That’s so critical. Like sure some podcasts are only relevant to current events but if i pick the first episode of a podcast, like the one that was released 10 years ago, you know which episode i want to listen to least? The one that was released yesterday. The one who’s intro I’ve heard 10 times right before I manually go down the huge list of episodes and select the damn next chronological episodes like some damn pleb.\n\nIf this was just some random app i stumbled upon then I’d be less harsh, but it’s by far one of the most popular podcast apps. Do other people listen to podcasts backwards? I just don’t understand.\n\nThere’s some setting that supposedly changes something about the order in which the episodes plays, I couldn’t tell what difference it made.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/review?id=888422857&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
